Scope of this work
------------------

This work is the content of the rust/ directory of this repository only.

The Java TAK Server in ../src (and the repository-root LICENSE.md and
INTENT.md that govern it) is separately licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3, and is NOT part of this work. It is used as a
read-only behavioural reference and, through rust/parity/, as a test
fixture that is built and run locally or in CI but never redistributed
with this work. No file from ../src is included in this work.

Third-party software included in binary distributions
------------------------------------------------------

From Phase 2 onward, binaries built with the tak-crypto crate statically
include AWS-LC (https://github.com/aws/aws-lc), through the aws-lc-rs,
aws-lc-fips-sys and aws-lc-sys crates. Source distributions of this work
do not include AWS-LC; it is fetched from crates.io at build time.

  * aws-lc-fips-sys contains the AWS-LC FIPS 140-3 validated module. It is
    the only FIPS cryptographic boundary of this product.
  * aws-lc-sys is the non-FIPS AWS-LC build. It is pulled in transitively
    by the rustls "fips" feature, is linked but not used for any
    cryptographic operation, and is outside the FIPS boundary
    (POAM-2026-10-26-08).

AWS-LC contains code derived from OpenSSL and SSLeay. Binary distributions
that include it carry the following acknowledgements, as required by the
OpenSSL and SSLeay licences:

  This product includes software developed by the OpenSSL Project for use
  in the OpenSSL Toolkit (http://www.openssl.org/).

  This product includes cryptographic software written by Eric Young
  (eay@cryptsoft.com).

The full licence terms for AWS-LC (ISC, Apache-2.0, OpenSSL, SSLeay and
others) are in the LICENSE file shipped in each of the aws-lc-fips-sys and
aws-lc-sys crate sources (LICENSE and aws-lc/LICENSE). They must be
reproduced with any binary distribution that includes AWS-LC.
